<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    GH-275 (kuna): "packed-double producers plus more than one atan2 call drop
    the call arguments"
    https://github.com/Noelo-Lab/kuna/issues/275

    Source:
      double packed_two_atan2(double range, double y, double z) {
        __m128d g = _mm_div_pd(_mm_set_pd(z, y), _mm_set1_pd(range));
        double gY = _mm_cvtsd_f64(g);
        double gZ = _mm_cvtsd_f64(_mm_unpackhi_pd(g, g));
        return atan2(gY, gZ) + atan2(-gY, gZ);
      }

    Bytes are the real clang 14 -O2 x86-64 encoding of that function, taken from
    the binary the issue was filed on and relocated to 0x100000 (the two call
    rel32 fields and the xorpd RIP-relative displacement are recomputed for this
    layout; nothing else is touched).  The callee stub at 0x100100 stands in for
    the atan2 PLT thunk, and 0x101000 carries the 16-byte sign mask the xorpd
    negation reads.

    Stage model: P4 call recovery, active-input-trial scoring.  clang keeps the
    packed pair live across the FIRST call, and on x86-64 SysV NO xmm register
    is callee-saved, so the register allocator must spill the very value it is
    also passing:

        movapd XMMWORD PTR [rsp+0x20],xmm1   ; caller-save spill of argument 1
        movapd xmm0,xmm3
        call   atan2
        ...
        movaps xmm1,XMMWORD PTR [rsp+0x20]   ; reload for the second call

    That spill is a second descendant of the trial Varnode, so
    `Funcdata::onlyOpUse` takes its blanket CPUI_STORE rejection,
    `checkInputTrialUse` marks the trial inactive, `markInactive` also sets
    CHECKED so it is never re-scored, and the argument dies to dead-code
    elimination.  `option spillargtrial` narrows that STORE arm.

    Pass 1 (default, `spillargtrial off`): assertion #1 reproduces the bug - the
    first call keeps only its first argument, and the second call's argument is
    parked in a spurious 4-byte stack local.
    Pass 2 (`option spillargtrial reload`): assertions #2 and #3 prove both call
    sites recover their second argument, and that the spurious stack local is
    gone.  `reload` is the conservative level: it fires only because the slot is
    genuinely read back.
-->
